WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.540 --> 00:00:02.001
- On June 12, 2016,

00:00:02.001 --> 00:00:03.894
I woke up like any other Sunday morning

00:00:03.894 --> 00:00:05.737
and like any other millennial

00:00:05.737 --> 00:00:07.467
instinctively checked my phone.

00:00:07.467 --> 00:00:08.814
I immediately saw two words splashed

00:00:08.814 --> 00:00:11.091
across news outlets and social media,

00:00:11.091 --> 00:00:12.841
Orlando and shooting.

00:00:13.879 --> 00:00:15.139
My first thought was oh it must be

00:00:15.139 --> 00:00:16.980
about the shooting that
happened last week.

00:00:16.980 --> 00:00:19.698
So I shrugged, wrap a rainbow
handkerchief around my neck,

00:00:19.698 --> 00:00:22.202
and traversed the few blocks
that separated my apartment

00:00:22.202 --> 00:00:25.647
from the start of the
Los Angeles Pride Parade.

00:00:25.647 --> 00:00:27.130
It was then and there surrounded by a sea

00:00:27.130 --> 00:00:30.604
of fellow LGBTQ marchers,
surrounded by family,

00:00:30.604 --> 00:00:32.174
that it became common knowledge

00:00:32.174 --> 00:00:33.911
that a very similar celebratory crowd

00:00:33.911 --> 00:00:36.446
of vibrant young people
had just hours before

00:00:36.446 --> 00:00:38.239
been gunned down at Pulse nightclub

00:00:38.239 --> 00:00:39.595
in what would be called
the worst mass shooting

00:00:39.595 --> 00:00:41.659
in modern US history.

00:00:41.659 --> 00:00:43.879
I realized throughout the
following week as my friends

00:00:43.879 --> 00:00:47.108
posted eulogies for victims
who they knew in the massacre

00:00:47.108 --> 00:00:49.085
that the degrees of separation
between these events

00:00:49.085 --> 00:00:51.324
and me don't exist anymore.

00:00:51.324 --> 00:00:53.796
In fact, I wondered if
they ever existed at all.

00:00:53.796 --> 00:00:55.464
And it dawned on me that the longest,

00:00:55.464 --> 00:00:58.949
most influential relationship
I never knew I had

00:00:58.949 --> 00:01:01.540
in my life is with mass shootings.

00:01:01.540 --> 00:01:03.128
These tragedies have
been brutally effective

00:01:03.128 --> 00:01:05.177
in shaping my world view.

00:01:05.177 --> 00:01:07.547
So I don't want to speak on this topic

00:01:07.547 --> 00:01:09.148
as some self purported expert

00:01:09.148 --> 00:01:10.698
like you'll see flooding your feeds,

00:01:10.698 --> 00:01:14.835
but from a more sincere,
experiential perspective.

00:01:14.835 --> 00:01:18.173
I can remember exactly where
I was and what I was doing

00:01:18.173 --> 00:01:20.926
for every major massacre in my lifetime.

00:01:20.926 --> 00:01:21.759
And more often than not

00:01:21.759 --> 00:01:24.730
the victims and the
perpetrators are around my age.

00:01:24.730 --> 00:01:26.523
I am stuck in a cyclical pattern

00:01:26.523 --> 00:01:27.845
of abuse in his relationship.

00:01:27.845 --> 00:01:29.247
But it wasn't always like this

00:01:29.247 --> 00:01:31.431
and it has gotten much, much worse.

00:01:31.431 --> 00:01:32.969
When I was five years old,

00:01:32.969 --> 00:01:34.555
a man crashed his pickup truck

00:01:34.555 --> 00:01:36.428
into a chain restaurant called Luby's

00:01:36.428 --> 00:01:38.588
about an hour and half from where I lived

00:01:38.588 --> 00:01:40.030
and shot and killed over 20 people.

00:01:40.030 --> 00:01:41.129
My father to calm my fears

00:01:41.129 --> 00:01:43.218
recounted an infamous school
shooting that had happened

00:01:43.218 --> 00:01:45.394
in the 1960s as we drove
passed the Clock Tower

00:01:45.394 --> 00:01:47.227
at the University of Texas.

00:01:47.227 --> 00:01:49.601
He pointed at it and reassured me

00:01:49.601 --> 00:01:51.883
that was the last time
something bad like this

00:01:51.883 --> 00:01:53.431
happened around here.

00:01:53.431 --> 00:01:56.691
These things don't happen
often so don't be scared.

00:01:56.691 --> 00:01:59.639
Little did he know at the time

00:01:59.639 --> 00:02:01.894
that he had only lived through
around 20 US mass shootings

00:02:01.894 --> 00:02:03.464
before I was born.

00:02:03.464 --> 00:02:06.198
By today I have lived
through over 100 and counting

00:02:06.198 --> 00:02:07.859
and it all began at Columbine.

00:02:07.859 --> 00:02:10.337
I was 13 years old and I
can vividly remember sitting

00:02:10.337 --> 00:02:11.365
in front of my television set

00:02:11.365 --> 00:02:12.746
in my living room watching the news replay

00:02:12.746 --> 00:02:15.481
the scenes of countless students
running out of the school

00:02:15.481 --> 00:02:16.975
with their hands on their heads.

00:02:16.975 --> 00:02:18.577
Teenagers my age were dangling

00:02:18.577 --> 00:02:21.024
from broken windows trying to escape.

00:02:21.024 --> 00:02:22.562
Columbine change everything.

00:02:22.562 --> 00:02:23.964
And as the adults argued politics

00:02:23.964 --> 00:02:26.373
we kids actually went
through a massive tonal shift

00:02:26.373 --> 00:02:27.404
when it came to our perspective

00:02:27.404 --> 00:02:29.453
on our peers and our culture and security

00:02:29.453 --> 00:02:31.853
and that's when I grew paranoid

00:02:31.853 --> 00:02:35.304
because our parents had
wars and we had Columbine.

00:02:35.304 --> 00:02:36.808
I remember schools
installing metal detectors

00:02:36.808 --> 00:02:39.009
at their entrances and I
remember that it became

00:02:39.009 --> 00:02:41.129
a common sick practical
joke for some idiot

00:02:41.129 --> 00:02:43.897
to call a bomb threat just to
watch everyone get evaluated.

00:02:43.897 --> 00:02:45.498
I remember rock music and video games

00:02:45.498 --> 00:02:47.411
and even the Internet being blamed.

00:02:47.411 --> 00:02:49.298
And if you wore a trench
coat you were a killer.

00:02:49.298 --> 00:02:51.937
We were very quick and eager
to turn on one another.

00:02:51.937 --> 00:02:54.644
Everyone debated about
who or what was at fault.

00:02:54.644 --> 00:02:55.786
And if history has taught us anything

00:02:55.786 --> 00:02:57.379
there is no easy answer.

00:02:57.379 --> 00:03:00.448
Kids were dead and nothing was done.

00:03:00.448 --> 00:03:03.044
And then 9/11 happened
and our generation went

00:03:03.044 --> 00:03:06.481
from cautiously skeptical
to absolutely terrified.

00:03:06.481 --> 00:03:08.721
Columbine ignited our
fears as young citizens

00:03:08.721 --> 00:03:13.163
then 911 defined it to be
rampant, righteous and unending.

00:03:13.163 --> 00:03:14.398
And why not? We were scared.

00:03:14.398 --> 00:03:16.773
You wanted answers but instead
of reaching for a common goal

00:03:16.773 --> 00:03:20.179
we split ourselves in two and
every conversation you had,

00:03:20.179 --> 00:03:22.229
every fight online you'll
see in the comments below

00:03:22.229 --> 00:03:23.830
and every election year we witness

00:03:23.830 --> 00:03:25.671
this endless back-and-forth
as more people die

00:03:25.671 --> 00:03:26.994
last resolutions are reached.

00:03:26.994 --> 00:03:28.734
Years later while I was
attending film school

00:03:28.734 --> 00:03:29.948
at the University of Southern California

00:03:29.948 --> 00:03:31.317
I was two weeks away
from publicly premiering

00:03:31.317 --> 00:03:33.275
a short film which had already wrapped

00:03:33.275 --> 00:03:35.340
when the deadliest attack
at that time happened

00:03:35.340 --> 00:03:38.468
on the opposite coast on
a campus much like mine.

00:03:38.468 --> 00:03:40.684
And in some twisted sense of timeliness

00:03:40.684 --> 00:03:43.435
my short film was a graphic
critique of school shootings.

00:03:43.435 --> 00:03:45.615
I remember a mother of one
of my friends walked up to me

00:03:45.615 --> 00:03:47.935
and remarked you should
watch what you make

00:03:47.935 --> 00:03:51.252
since it looks like your
kind are prone to violence.

00:03:51.252 --> 00:03:52.878
Virginia Tech like any other massacre

00:03:52.878 --> 00:03:55.317
involving a wide array of players
from different backgrounds

00:03:55.317 --> 00:03:57.110
whether it was racial,
religious, cultural,

00:03:57.110 --> 00:03:59.884
brought forth and ugliness
that direct affected me

00:03:59.884 --> 00:04:01.366
for the first time.

00:04:01.366 --> 00:04:02.907
And as we mourned the dead it struck me

00:04:02.907 --> 00:04:04.948
that every time that this happens

00:04:04.948 --> 00:04:06.480
it not only opens up an opportunity

00:04:06.480 --> 00:04:08.560
to advance personal and political agendas,

00:04:08.560 --> 00:04:10.800
it becomes top priority
for most of us to do so.

00:04:10.800 --> 00:04:13.674
And yet again kids were
dead and nothing was done.

00:04:13.674 --> 00:04:15.716
You have Omaha, Binghamton,
Fort Hood twice.

00:04:15.716 --> 00:04:18.148
Fort hood in the same town

00:04:18.148 --> 00:04:20.461
as that Luby's cafeteria that
was shot up in my childhood.

00:04:20.461 --> 00:04:22.996
Schools, malls, churches,
post offices, military bases,

00:04:22.996 --> 00:04:26.570
a grocery store parking lot in Tucson.

00:04:26.570 --> 00:04:28.395
And then a movie theater in Aurora

00:04:28.395 --> 00:04:30.620
during a midnight screening
of The Dark Knight Rises.

00:04:30.620 --> 00:04:33.323
Where was I? Waiting to
attend a midnight screening

00:04:33.323 --> 00:04:35.157
of The Dark Knight Rises.

00:04:35.157 --> 00:04:36.384
We all could have been those victims

00:04:36.384 --> 00:04:38.600
excitedly waiting to watch a
blockbuster on opening night.

00:04:38.600 --> 00:04:39.827
No one was safe.

00:04:39.827 --> 00:04:41.979
And then later that year over 20 people,

00:04:41.979 --> 00:04:43.973
the majority being children
on the first grade,

00:04:43.973 --> 00:04:46.029
were shot and killed at Sandy Hook,

00:04:46.029 --> 00:04:47.113
our little brothers and sisters,

00:04:47.113 --> 00:04:49.186
our own children gunned down.

00:04:49.186 --> 00:04:50.775
My gut reaction was well now things

00:04:50.775 --> 00:04:52.959
will definitely have to change.

00:04:52.959 --> 00:04:54.545
But it did not.

00:04:54.545 --> 00:04:57.392
Little kids were dead
and nothing was done.

00:04:57.392 --> 00:05:01.153
Santa Monica, Santa Barbara,
Marysville, Umpqua, Charleston,

00:05:01.153 --> 00:05:02.348
I apologize if I'm forgetting some

00:05:02.348 --> 00:05:03.910
but there's just too many to count.

00:05:03.910 --> 00:05:05.505
So many that I am becoming so used

00:05:05.505 --> 00:05:06.629
to turning from passionate rage

00:05:06.629 --> 00:05:08.231
to desensitize resignation on a dime.

00:05:08.231 --> 00:05:10.823
I only shrugged. I screamed
and then I shrugged.

00:05:10.823 --> 00:05:12.035
And then I forgot.

00:05:12.035 --> 00:05:13.932
Our interconnectedness
not only as a nation

00:05:13.932 --> 00:05:15.622
but also as an international community.

00:05:15.622 --> 00:05:18.046
The Internet, social
media and bullet holes

00:05:18.046 --> 00:05:20.223
are like the connected dots
that link our generation

00:05:20.223 --> 00:05:21.635
beyond each of the shores.

00:05:21.635 --> 00:05:23.715
Paris my second home
where my mother has lived

00:05:23.715 --> 00:05:25.685
for over 17 years was hit by a series

00:05:25.685 --> 00:05:28.406
of unfathomable terrorist attacks.

00:05:28.406 --> 00:05:32.597
And my immediate bleak
thought was my mother is dead.

00:05:32.597 --> 00:05:33.453
Thankfully she was unharmed

00:05:33.453 --> 00:05:36.458
but we have come to such a
low point as a global society

00:05:36.458 --> 00:05:38.260
where we assume the absolute worse

00:05:38.260 --> 00:05:39.630
because it's how we already view

00:05:39.630 --> 00:05:41.615
one another as human beings.

00:05:41.615 --> 00:05:43.910
And then less than a month
later San Bernardino happened

00:05:43.910 --> 00:05:45.273
and my mother returned the favor

00:05:45.273 --> 00:05:47.178
and had to call me to see if I was okay.

00:05:47.178 --> 00:05:49.438
Our entire office on Sunset Boulevard

00:05:49.438 --> 00:05:52.293
heard the sirens driving
eastward to San Bernardino

00:05:52.293 --> 00:05:54.288
less than an hour away.

00:05:54.288 --> 00:05:56.300
In the following week we'd
hold a security meeting

00:05:56.300 --> 00:05:58.509
on what to do in an
active shooter situation.

00:05:58.509 --> 00:06:00.358
What was once video games and trench coats

00:06:00.358 --> 00:06:02.296
has morphed into the red flag dechoir

00:06:02.296 --> 00:06:03.986
for politicians who have ensured,

00:06:03.986 --> 00:06:06.083
especially with our upcoming election,

00:06:06.083 --> 00:06:08.404
that we are a country solely
operating on our fear.

00:06:08.404 --> 00:06:10.661
We have let the politicians
and talking heads

00:06:10.661 --> 00:06:12.615
and online forums dictate a conversation

00:06:12.615 --> 00:06:14.575
that our generation needs to have

00:06:14.575 --> 00:06:16.824
about our role in the
fight against violence.

00:06:16.824 --> 00:06:18.475
We grew up on these my shootings.

00:06:18.475 --> 00:06:20.580
The victims and unfortunately the shooters

00:06:20.580 --> 00:06:23.347
are people we all personally know.

00:06:23.347 --> 00:06:26.106
Orlando provided a
spotlight on a real issue

00:06:26.106 --> 00:06:28.419
this disconnect between
those who write the narrative

00:06:28.419 --> 00:06:30.436
and those who are actually living it.

00:06:30.436 --> 00:06:33.587
Most of our leaders are
not what the victims were

00:06:33.587 --> 00:06:36.921
primarily LGBTQ LatinX, black and young.

00:06:36.921 --> 00:06:39.365
In fact many, many a politician

00:06:39.365 --> 00:06:41.910
aim to marginalize those groups today.

00:06:41.910 --> 00:06:43.305
We are passionate and over-educated,

00:06:43.305 --> 00:06:45.953
but desensitized and underrepresented

00:06:45.953 --> 00:06:47.515
and thus we become divided

00:06:47.515 --> 00:06:48.814
just like the generations before us.

00:06:48.814 --> 00:06:51.295
But instead we need to
consider shutting the fuck up

00:06:51.295 --> 00:06:54.033
for a second and actually
doing something about it.

00:06:54.033 --> 00:06:57.056
The patrons of Pulse were
targeted because of who they were.

00:06:57.056 --> 00:06:58.314
They were queer people of color

00:06:58.314 --> 00:07:00.286
and US millennials out there all know

00:07:00.286 --> 00:07:01.941
and love someone from those backgrounds

00:07:01.941 --> 00:07:04.718
and not all politicians do.

00:07:04.718 --> 00:07:07.133
It's fine to share their
speeches in your opinions

00:07:07.133 --> 00:07:08.455
even about this very video,

00:07:08.455 --> 00:07:11.758
but posting in the infinite
soapbox that is the Internet

00:07:11.758 --> 00:07:13.208
is like prayer without action.

00:07:13.208 --> 00:07:15.010
Contact your elected officials

00:07:15.010 --> 00:07:16.452
because eventually we're gonna become

00:07:16.452 --> 00:07:17.641
those elected officials.

00:07:17.641 --> 00:07:18.988
Some merely shrugging at politics

00:07:18.988 --> 00:07:20.335
instead of actively participating in it

00:07:20.335 --> 00:07:21.954
will not change the game.

00:07:21.954 --> 00:07:23.811
Let's get up all in their business

00:07:23.811 --> 00:07:25.932
because if Orlando has taught us anything

00:07:25.932 --> 00:07:27.933
it's that they need to know

00:07:27.933 --> 00:07:29.472
that we cannot watch
any more of our friends

00:07:29.472 --> 00:07:30.874
and love ones die.

00:07:30.874 --> 00:07:33.155
And I'll be damned if kids who
are watching this right now

00:07:33.155 --> 00:07:34.709
will grow up to be another statistic

00:07:34.709 --> 00:07:36.360
because we blindly join a system

00:07:36.360 --> 00:07:37.568
that loves to argue about problems

00:07:37.568 --> 00:07:39.793
but refuses to produce actual results.

00:07:39.793 --> 00:07:42.301
Mass shootings they have been my longest

00:07:42.301 --> 00:07:44.349
most intelligible relationship, yes,

00:07:44.349 --> 00:07:48.376
but from this moment on it
will be I who defines it.

00:07:48.376 --> 00:07:50.234
And when I look back on June 12, 2016,

00:07:50.234 --> 00:07:53.208
I want not only remember
the deaths of the innocent,

00:07:53.208 --> 00:07:56.638
but what we did to finally make a change.

00:07:56.638 --> 00:07:59.493
And finally to the LGBT community

00:07:59.493 --> 00:08:02.787
know that you are brave and
that you are strong and loved

00:08:02.787 --> 00:08:04.870
and that we are with you.

